      "name": "introducing_a_boolean_column_is_not_a_change_on_rows_that_lack_it",
      "comment": "Boolean fields compare by truthiness. The snapshot predating a boolean column has no value for it (absent, or null once re-serialized); the snapshot after it carries an explicit false on every row that is not flagged. Reporting that as an edit flags the entire corpus the first time a post-column snapshot is diffed against a pre-column one — 210 cards on 6be2c64e->5216a20b alone. TypeScript had this rule from the start; Python compared None != False and reported all of them.",
